  "implementation": [
    "Find bounded base UV with the existing closest-point kernel. Decompose residuals through a skew-aware differential basis, map normalized foot coordinates, then continue exterior residuals with native target parameter derivatives. Retain native parameter-domain scaling and normal heights.",
    "Prepare signed and exchanged parameter frames for corner/edge picks. Keep SDK corner-only orientation distinct from actual command edge orientation. Explicit command normal directions are unitized; the public point API retains vector magnitude.",
    "Capture selectable immutable surface/face references. AutoAdjust uses the shared B-rep shrink interval policy and delegates exact restriction to the existing surface_segments backend (usd-brep when native-smlib is enabled). Native UV normals ignore B-rep face reversal.",
    "Share curve/surface fitting, rigid pose generation, grip-owner precedence, group bounds and atomic document edit paths with Flow. Preserve zero cofactor directions when averaging a tangent-constrained rigid frame. Retain complete owner/grip/group/selection state through Undo and Redo.",
    "Register FlowAlongSrf and FlowAlongSurface. Support script references, explicit face indices, frame overrides, Plane input, normal constraints, remembered options, copy preferences, source-first selection, grip selection, and one history edit.",
    "Use shared immutable preview cages/cache for objects and grips. Interactive surface/face picks, two-corner or three-point temporary planes, target-view CPlane normal defaults, reference invalidation, cancellation and commit leave geometry staging in the command layer."
  ],
